    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Hi @brandon-b-miller ,\nBy \"non-deterministic,\" I mean that this synchronization issue occurs only with certain Parquet files of mine, while it doesn't manifest with others. Let me summarize the points I've made above:\n- **In the initial and primary set of profiling results**, when reading column C from Parquet file A, `read_parquet` from different streams are synchronizing with one another. As a result, there is no actual pipelining taking place. This synchronization persists throughout the entire reading process of **Parquet file A**.\n- In contrast, **the last figure**, which depict the expected behavior, show that when reading column C from Parquet file B, the pipeline functions as intended. Throughout the entire reading of **Parquet file B**, such time-consuming synchronization issues are consistently absent.\n\nIn conclusion, this synchronization behavior from GIL seems to be correlated with the specific Parquet file being read (in my case)",
