    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Hi @brandon-b-miller \nIt appears to me that this is a stream synchronization issue, specifically involving unnecessary synchronization with other streams in different threads. To conduct a sanity check, I took the following steps:\n- Enabling PTDS: I attempted to enable the ptds using the `./build.sh --ptds libcudf pylibcudf`. Unfortunately, this did not yield any improvements. In the PTDS, there is a CUDA synchronization call named `cudaStreamSynchronize_ptsz`. However, I was unable to find any documentation regarding this particular call.\n\nHere is the same thing happening with ptds enabled:\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/483a83ca-9aff-4761-8b2c-37583ef249e9)\n\n---\n\n- Comparison with C++ Implementation: I also implemented the same functionality in C++ libcudf to determine if the unnecessary synchronization was exclusive to pylibcudf. After testing, I concluded that the issue is specific to pylibcudf. When using the C++ version of libcudf, I did not observe any synchronization issues originating from the RMM device buffer. Everything is expected without any time gap sync-ing:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8668177c-97e8-4487-949b-ec6ddd77f498)\n\nHowever, I am still not able to workaround this issue and I think I will now check with the device buffer cpython code :(",
