    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "> Enabling PTDS: I attempted to enable the ptds using the ./build.sh --ptds libcudf pylibcudf. Unfortunately, this did not yield any improvements. In the PTDS, there is a CUDA synchronization call named cudaStreamSynchronize_ptsz. However, I was unable to find any documentation regarding this particular call.\n\nI think you would need to _also_ compile RMM Python with PTDS.\n\n\nThanks for this detailed investigation. It looks like it is (as you note) not sufficient just to pass streams through the IO API. Particularly, when, in pylibcudf we take ownership of the `unique_ptr<table>/unique_ptr<column>` produced by the `read_xxx` routine, we currently _do not_ pass a stream through. Therefore we call rmm's `DeviceBuffer.c_from_unique_ptr` with the default stream as argument: \n\nhttps://github.com/rapidsai/rmm/blob/ef8eca48008ff8239df9e628b1317f32ab7ee9de/python/rmm/rmm/pylibrmm/device_buffer.pyx#L199-L210\n\nAnd this syncs the stream.",
